From 155c127c338ceb595ba86dc70c83575de7f865b7 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Josep Torra <n770galaxy@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 21 Oct 2026 02:56:50 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 07/12] ##arch: Decode and assemble the whole USSE instruction
 set

Sync the clean-room core: the form table now covers every encoding
Imagination's own disassembler considers valid on the SGX545, in all 32
opcode classes (float arithmetic, texture sampling, pack/unpack, the
integer and dual-issue groups, the special and control class), held to
0 wrong against it and assembling back. lapc, a jump to the link
register, is typed as a return (a conditional one when predicated).

test/db/asm/usse: add control forms whose operand fields the earlier
decoders did not decode in general (idf/wdf beyond drc1, predicated
lapc, smlsi, emitpds, ci, cfi, lock).
